  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure a block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> lying on a horizontal surface is pulled by a force F acting at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, with horizontal. For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>, the block will just start to move for the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>: [Given g <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0040_6a49d9abfc4e.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 259px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>",
